ing more than a point or two from the combined estimate.", "watch": "Any independent or additional polling confirming Leonard's competitiveness, or major outside spending against Carey, would narrow the race.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Mike Carey (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Ohio's 15th District leans Republican by about five points, and first-term incumbent Mike Carey is seeking re-election with a substantial financial advantage, having raised roughly $3.3 million to Democrat Don Leonard's $0.6 million. Most expert raters call the race Likely R, though a few see it as Lean R, and prediction markets give Carey about a 78 percent chance of winning. Leonard has kept the race within single digits in Democratic-sponsored polling, and Carey has drawn criticism for votes on SNAP, Medicaid, and education funding. National Democrats have also targeted the district with advertising. Still, the structural advantages favor Carey, and the forecast expects him to win by roughly six points with meaningful uncertainty, keeping this a competitive but Republican-leaning contest.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1732, "margin": -5.63}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1799, "margin": -6.0}]}